      "message": "In `SendBootromCommandSha` and `SendBootromCommandAes`, you construct the header using raw pointer arithmetic (`uint8_t *cmd_iv \u003d cmd_ptr + kStatusHeaderSize + kWrappedCommandSize;`). This is hard to read and prone to off-by-one errors.\n\nSince you already use `__attribute__((packed))` successfully in `ec_protocol_defs.h`, you can define your Secure Channel headers the same way.\n\n**The Struct:**\n\n```c\nstruct SecureCommandShaHeader {\n    uint8_t command_id \u003d EgisBootrom::CMD_SECURE_WRAPPED;\n    uint8_t algo \u003d CRYPTO_SHA_256;\n    uint32_t payload_len; // Ensure this is converted to LE before assignment\n    std::array\u003cuint8_t, 32\u003e hash;\n} __attribute__((packed));\n\n```\n\n**Simplified `SendBootromCommandSha` Setup:**\n\n```c\nSecureCommandShaHeader header;\nheader.payload_len \u003d htole32(static_cast\u003cuint32_t\u003e(data.size()));\nSHA256(data.data(), data.size(), header.hash.data());\n\nstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e cmd;\ncmd.reserve(sizeof(header) + data.size());\nconst auto* header_bytes \u003d reinterpret_cast\u003cconst uint8_t*\u003e(\u0026header);\ncmd.append_range(std::span(header_bytes, sizeof(header)));\ncmd.append_range(data);\n\n```",
