      "message": "In `bootrom.cc`, this bitwise shifting block appears **9 times** to serialize 32-bit integers into the command vectors:\n\n```c\n// Appears in WriteReg, ReadReg, BackupFlash, ReadFlash, EraseFlash, WriteFlash...\nfor (int i \u003d 0; i \u003c 4; i++)\n    cmd.push_back((addr \u003e\u003e (i * 8)) \u0026 0xFF);\n\n```\n\nSince you are already building a `ReadLittleEndian` helper, you can build its exact opposite to handle this safely and cleanly.\n\n**The Helper:**\n\n```c\ntemplate \u003cstd::integral T\u003e\nvoid AppendLittleEndian(std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e\u0026 vec, T value) {\n    if constexpr (std::endian::native !\u003d std::endian::little) {\n        value \u003d std::byteswap(value);\n    }\n    const auto* bytes \u003d reinterpret_cast\u003cconst uint8_t*\u003e(\u0026value);\n    // C++23 feature: append_range\n    vec.append_range(std::span(bytes, sizeof(T))); \n}\n\n```\n\n**Before (`EraseFlash`):**\n\n```c\nstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e data;\ndata.push_back(EgisBootrom::CMD_FLASH_ERASE);\nuint32_t addr \u003d EgisBootrom::FLASH_BASE_ADDR + offset;\nfor (int i \u003d 0; i \u003c 4; i++) data.push_back((addr \u003e\u003e (i * 8)) \u0026 0xFF);\nfor (int i \u003d 0; i \u003c 4; i++) data.push_back((size \u003e\u003e (i * 8)) \u0026 0xFF);\n\n```\n\n**After:**\n\n```c\nstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e data \u003d { EgisBootrom::CMD_FLASH_ERASE };\nAppendLittleEndian(data, EgisBootrom::FLASH_BASE_ADDR + offset);\nAppendLittleEndian(data, size);\n\n```",
