      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Replace \"Magic Sleeps\" with Status Polling for Flash Writes** The fixed 10ms delays in `WriteEnable()`, `SetSr1()`, and `WriteFlash()` are risky. If the physical flash chip takes longer than 10ms to complete a page program or register write (due to chip wear or temperature), the next operation will overlap and potentially corrupt the flash. **Suggestion:** Instead of `sleep_for(10ms)`, standard practice is to read the SPI Flash Status Register 1 (SR1) in a `while` loop, checking the **WIP (Write In Progress) bit** (usually Bit 0). Keep polling until WIP goes to 0\\. This guarantees the operation is finished and optimizes speed by proceeding the exact millisecond the chip is ready.",
