      "message": "Currently, there are several places where integers are extracted from USB responses using raw pointer arithmetic and `std::memcpy`. This assumes the host machine is little-endian and bypasses bounds checking.\n\n**Locations to update in `bootrom.cc`:**\n\n* `GetBootromInfo()`: Parsing `version`, `max_size`, and `max_fw_upgrade_size`.  \n* `GetFlashInfo()`: Parsing `flash_size`.  \n* `ReadReg()`: Parsing `value_out`.  \n* `SendBootromCommandAes()`: Parsing `rsp_wrapped_len`.\n\n**Suggestion:** Since we are compiling with C++23, we can use `\u003cbit\u003e` and `std::span` to create a zero-cost, type-safe, and bounds-checked parsing helper.\n\n**1\\. Add this helper function (e.g., in `bootrom.cc` or a shared utility header):**\n\n```c\n#include \u003cbit\u003e\n#include \u003cconcepts\u003e\n#include \u003ccstring\u003e\n#include \u003cexpected\u003e\n#include \u003cspan\u003e\n\ntemplate \u003cstd::integral T\u003e\nstd::expected\u003cT, int\u003e ReadLittleEndian(std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e buffer) {\n    if (buffer.size() \u003c sizeof(T)) return std::unexpected(-1);\n\n    T value;\n    std::memcpy(\u0026value, buffer.data(), sizeof(T));\n    \n    if constexpr (std::endian::native !\u003d std::endian::little) {\n        value \u003d std::byteswap(value);\n    }\n    return value;\n}\n\n```\n\n**2\\. Example replacement in `GetBootromInfo()`:**\n\n*Before:*\n\n```c\nif (resp-\u003esize() \u003e\u003d 12) {\n    uint32_t version, max_size, max_fw_upgrade_size;\n    std::memcpy(\u0026version, resp-\u003edata(), 4);\n    std::memcpy(\u0026max_size, resp-\u003edata() + 4, 4);\n    std::memcpy(\u0026max_fw_upgrade_size, resp-\u003edata() + 8, 4);\n    // ...\n\n```\n\n*After:*\n\n```c\nstd::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e payload \u003d resp.value();\n\nauto version \u003d ReadLittleEndian\u003cuint32_t\u003e(payload);\nauto max_size \u003d ReadLittleEndian\u003cuint32_t\u003e(payload.subspan(4));\nauto max_fw_up_size \u003d ReadLittleEndian\u003cuint32_t\u003e(payload.subspan(8));\n\nif (!version || !max_size || !max_fw_up_size) {\n    std::println(stderr, \"[ERROR] Truncated response in GetBootromInfo\");\n    return -1;\n}\n\nstd::println(\"Bootrom Version: 0x{:x}\", version.value());\nstd::println(\"Max Command Size: {} bytes\", max_size.value());\nstd::println(\"Max FW Upgrade Size: {} bytes\", max_fw_up_size.value());\n\n```\n\n**3\\. Example replacement in `SendBootromCommandAes()`:**\n\n*Before:*\n\n```c\nuint32_t rsp_wrapped_len \u003d 0;\nstd::memcpy(\u0026rsp_wrapped_len, \u0026ret[kStatusHeaderSize], sizeof(rsp_wrapped_len));\n\n```\n\n*After:*\n\n```c\nauto len_res \u003d ReadLittleEndian\u003cuint32_t\u003e(std::span(ret).subspan(kStatusHeaderSize));\nif (!len_res) return std::unexpected(-4); // Or appropriate error code\nuint32_t rsp_wrapped_len \u003d len_res.value();\n\n```",
